<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21273] sanity test_0e: directories are on the same MDT with ZFS MDTs</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21273</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_0e fails intermittently with "directories are on the same MDT N=N". This is the same symptom as &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17223" title="sanity test_0e: directories are on the same MDT 2=2" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17223"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17223&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, which was closed as Cannot Reproduce. This ticket has the root cause.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_0e assumes mkdir in ROOT places the two directories round-robin. The client only uses round-robin while MDT free space is within lmv.*.qos_threshold_rr (5% by default). ZFS MDTs only estimate their free inodes, so even empty MDTs are far apart: 5.1M vs 7.4M inodes (about 31%) on a 4-MDT, 2-MDS ZFS setup. LMV then uses weighted-random QoS placement, and the two mkdirs sometimes land on the same MDT. On that setup it failed 3 of 20 runs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: set lmv.*.qos_threshold_rr=100 for the duration of the test and restore it with stack_trap. With that change it passed 20 of 20 runs.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>&amp;lt;distro/arch&amp;gt;, ZFS backend, 2 MDS / 4 MDT</environment>
